# x-residual-moves-client: callers of the four residual files -> core methods (NOT applied: see why)

Why this is a fragment and not an edit: every caller is a file other tasks own (ipc-sessions.ts: s2a-ts-api-sessions;
ipc-window-settings.ts: s2a-ts-api-settings; model-bootstrap.ts: x-residual-verdicts; ipc.ts is a desktop hot file), and the core
does not serve the six methods yet (DesktopResidualService is not registered, the six names are in SERVICE_PENDING). The
AttachmentHost implementation exists (mixdog-core-session session/attachments.rs DesktopAttachmentHost, g35-fu-x); its
registration and the removal of the six SERVICE_PENDING names are written in native/core/crates/pending-wire/g35-fu-x.wire section 1.
Switching a caller first would lose the attachment open, the font list and the link resolution. Deleting a file first would
break its caller's import. So the four files stay byte for byte until the lines below are applied, in this order, by the same
wiring that applies g35-fu-x.wire section 1 (apply that section first).

## 1. system-fonts.ts + system-fonts.test.mjs: delete
ipc-window-settings.ts: drop `import { listSystemFonts } from './system-fonts'`; replace
  handle(DESKTOP_IPC.listSystemFonts, () => listSystemFonts());
with
  handle(DESKTOP_IPC.listSystemFonts, async () => ((await core.call('desktop/fonts/list', {})) as { families: string[] }).families);
(`core` = the window's ProtocolConnection, passed from ipc.ts the way registerNotificationIpc gets `core: protocol`; with no
connection the call fails as notifications do.) The core listing answers [] on failure, as the TS one did.

## 2. session-attachments.ts + transcript-file-links.ts + both tests: delete
ipc-sessions.ts: drop the import of './session-attachments'; replace the readSessionAttachment handler body with
  const sid = requiredSessionId(sessionId);
  const { viewName, attachment, dataUrl, bytes } = await core.call('desktop/attachment/resolve', { sessionId: sid, attachmentId });
  return { name: viewName, mimeType: attachment.mimeType, size: bytes, dataUrl };
A refusal arrives with code `file-download:not-linked|not-found|changed`; map it back with FileDownloadError (shared/file-downloads)
where the paired-device download path reads fileDownloadErrorReason. `stageSessionAttachment` has no caller in the tree
today; `desktop/attachment/stage` { sessionId, attachmentId } -> { path, attachment } serves a later caller. `requestedLinkPath` / `resolveLinkedPath` had no
caller outside the two files: the core methods desktop/link/resolve and desktop/link/resolvePath serve later callers.
session-history-boundary.test.mjs: remove 'main/session-attachments.ts' from the expected `readSessionHistory` list (the DesktopService
`readSessionHistory` / `readSessionTranscript?` members then have no reader in main: drop them from desktop-service-contract.ts,
desktop-service-client.ts and the SERVICE_OPERATION list with the sessionLane read if nothing else calls them).

## 3. workflow-config.ts: delete
Only `objectRecord` is used (model-bootstrap.ts, import line 9); `parseJsonc` / `readJsoncFile` have no caller (core:
desktop/workflowConfig/read). Put `const record = (v: unknown) => v && typeof v === 'object' && !Array.isArray(v) ? v as Record<string, unknown> : null;`
in model-bootstrap.ts in place of the import, then delete the file.

## Parity checklist (TS case -> Rust twin in mixdog-core-domains desktop_residual_tests.rs)
session-attachments.test: names attachments from user rows only, legacy images -> a_session_names_its_attachments_from_user_rows_only_legacy_images_included;
  reads by id for its own session only -> an_attachment_reads_by_id_for_its_own_session_and_for_no_other;
  compacted history names it -> an_attachment_only_the_compacted_history_names_opens_and_another_sessions_id_is_still_refused;
  store lost or corrupted -> a_named_attachment_the_store_no_longer_holds_or_holds_corrupted_is_not_served;
transcript-file-links.test: href decoding -> an_href_is_decoded_the_way_markdown_link_decodes_it_and_a_web_link_names_no_file (+ windows_hrefs_resolve_with_node_win32_rules);
  resolve against the session folder / UNC never -> a_link_resolves_against_the_session_folder_and_network_paths_never_resolve;
  task report / room speech attachments -> a_task_reports_and_a_room_speechs_returned_files_are_attachments_and_other_notices_carry_none;
system-fonts.test: sorted unique families -> font_listings_become_sorted_unique_family_names; no listing -> a_platform_without_a_listing_answers_an_empty_list_and_free_text_stays;
workflow-config (no TS test): jsonc_comments_and_trailing_commas_are_read_and_strings_are_left_alone, a_jsonc_file_that_is_missing_empty_or_nul_filled_holds_no_settings;
stage -> an_attachment_stages_under_the_temp_directory_with_a_previewable_name; sessionId trim -> a_session_id_is_trimmed_and_holds_only_id_characters.
Exported functions -> Rust (desktop_residual.rs): requiredAttachmentId -> attachment_id_shape (inside read_session_attachment);
readSessionAttachment -> read_session_attachment; attachmentViewName -> attachment_view_name; stageSessionAttachment -> stage_session_attachment;
NETWORK_PATH / resolveLinkedPath / requestedLinkPath -> resolve_linked_path / requested_link_path; sessionAttachments -> session_attachments;
parseJsonc / readJsoncFile -> parse_jsonc / read_jsonc_file; objectRecord -> object_record (and the local `record` in model-bootstrap.ts);
parseFontFamilies / listSystemFonts -> parse_font_families / list_system_fonts; the service dispatch -> the_service_answers_links_attachments_and_settings.
